<title>FRANCE: CDR sells 14.9 mln Rhone-Poulenc shares.</title>
<headline>CDR sells 14.9 mln Rhone-Poulenc shares.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Consortium de Realisation said it had placed its 14.9 million shares in Rhone-Poulenc, or a 4.6 percent stake, with institutional investors.</p>
<p>It did not communciate the price.</p>
<p>The placement was executed by Societe Generale.  </p>
<p>A CDR spokesman said the price would not be revealed until the operation was completed.</p>
<p>The deal is conditional upon Rhone-Poulenc's core share holders not using their pre-emption rights. These shareholders are AGF, Societe Generale, BNP, AXA, Fiat and Credit Suisse.</p>
</text>
